# Approximations: fits in real arithmetic, rounded and re-optimised
# coefficients, measured as evaluated, ranked by error and cost.

# sin on [-pi/2, pi/2] in f32: odd, so x*P(x^2); with and without
# exact endpoints (sin(pi/2) = 1)
approx sin(x) in -pi/2..pi/2 degree 5..9 norational nosplit noreduce
approx sin(x) in -pi/2..pi/2 degree 5..9 keep endpoints norational nosplit noreduce
s(x: f32 in -1.57079637..1.57079637) = sin(x)
error ap3 ~ s
cost ap3
approx more 2

# range reduction: exp as 2^k * P(r), 2^k built in the exponent field
approx exp(x) in -10..10 ulp 2 nosplit norational list 2 as c

# log by exponent/mantissa split; relative error through the zero at 1
approx log(x) in 0.5..100 relative ulp 2 nosplit norational list 2

# atan: odd, reciprocal for |x| > 1, sign by copysign
approx atan(x) in -10..10 ulp 2 nosplit norational list 2

# 1/sqrt: polynomial seed and a Newton step, and the bit hack
approx 1/sqrt(x) in 0.01..100 ulp 2 nosplit norational list 3

# cos near pi/2, relative: the identity sin(pi/2 - x) with pi/2 in two
# parts is the one that keeps relative accuracy
approx cos(x) in 0..pi/2 relative norational nosplit list 3

# rational fits win when division is cheap
model cheapdiv : gt1030 { fdiv: 2 }
use cheapdiv
approx tan(x) in -1.4..1.4 ulp 8 nosplit noreduce list 3
use gt1030

# any function; real arithmetic; a two-piece split
g(x) = 1/(1 + x^2)
approx g in -1..1 as real degree 2..4 list 3 nosplit
approx exp(-x*x) in -2..2 degree 6 norational list 3
approx sqrt(x) in 0..1 degree 2 nosplit norational noreduce

# f64: sin by quadrant with a three-part pi/2 (33-bit pieces)
approx sin(x) in -100..100 as f64 ulp 2 nosplit norational list 1
